// S~S  SimpleSal signal starts  S~S

// [Agency FSM Algorithm.note]          search in ssTEA source files for a reference to this file.
//
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   This is the API the App uses to transfer ownership of Agency to ssTEA.  This transfer of
   Agency ownership happens during the App's "loop" (Arduino) or "idle" (RTOS) function.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The special name for this API indicates the main view the App has of ssTEA software.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   void ssTEA_Agency_Root (TimeUnitsBig_t MicrosSinceLast, TimeUnitsBig_t MillisSinceLast);

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The Agency algorithm's Root refers to Next.
        [.\SimpleSal\ssDocs\ssTEA\Agency Next Algorithm.note]
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   This note does not discuss the algorithm used by the implementation in ssTEA to store
   event data per event or the algorithm used to store and manipulate an Event's daa.
   The Next function may be rewritten to a different model, without changing Agency Root.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The ssTEA source file also contain comments about the local algorithm's implementation.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   ssE_pEvInfo_t ssA_EvAg_AgencyNext (ssE_pEvInfo_t pEvInfo, ssE_EvType_t  eventType)
//
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Control of the flow of execution, or agency, is granted by the user by calling Agency Root.
   This function performs the highest-level algorithms for managing events.   Is this efficient?
   Let's say that all that is happening in the embedded system is calls to Agency Root, and it is
   spending all of its time going through the complex "if" statement below, waiting for events.
   Truth: The user not using ssTEA would be making all of the same choices while waiting.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Several rules and features are in conflict with each other:
        AgencyNext only returns either a NULL pointer or a pointer to an Event that needs attention,
        the rules for agency prohibit running one event twice in the same planck,
        events are triggered by a prioritized set of classifications (hot interrupt, data, time)
   The resolution of these conflicting influences is hidden within the Agency Root function.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   rules for when events may be run
    interrupt-triggered and data-triggered events are always run on the next planck boundary,
    regardless of pace selection and pace precision.  They must wait for the next planck so ssTEA
    Events cannot starve the App and Host OS; Agency is returned to the Host OS for a turn.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    The difference between interrupts and data is that all interrupts are run before any Data/Time,
    in the same Planck.  However, an interrupt or data Event that signals an interrupt or data event
    will not see that Event granted Agency until the next planck.  This prevents infinite loops.
    pace | TimeEv | pace | TimeEv | IntEv-signal | planck | IntEv DataEv-signal | planck | DataEv.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Interrupt/Data events may signal for the occurence of a Time Event with Current Time or earlier,
    AgencyNext will find the event and grant it Agency, as early as the next pace period boundary;
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Claiming dominion over Time requires that all of Time be accounted for; if you refuse to make
    a choice, that action is the result of making a choice.  All Time outside ssTEA is the App's.
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ssA_EvAg_RootMath_Entry ();
//
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Rule: Agency only executes if Time is running; no Time means no Agency. Change takes Time.
    while Time is not running, statistics are not maintained about Time at the ssTEA level.
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    A "32-bit unsigned long int" is the base counter type, a maximum value of (4,294,967,295).
    that 32-bit microsecond counter turns into 4,294-second counter, which is around 71 mins.
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Relying on Current Time in every situation allows software to not care about the true Time.
    Software such as SimpleSal will use this concept to construct Events simulating any Time.
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ssT tracks Current Time in a Time Variable; ssT can += (N usecs) until Time's days overflow
      (see ssT but the range of values for days is probably 0-999, so your Time context may fit).
    After the timeOp, TimeCurr represents the current time throughout ssTEA, accurate to N usecs.
    Perform the TimeCurr calculation at this moment as it allows for variation and manipulation.
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    if (ssTEA_control.TimeState != ssTEA_state_running)
//
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Time is running and measured independent of the Agency state of the ssTEA Agency Root FSM.
    some categories of Time only exist or result from computations while Agencying.
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    if (ssTEA_control.Agency_state != ssTEA_state_running)
//
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    There is an FSM running that cycles through EvTypes (Ireq, Data, Time), and in addition,
    there is an FSM running that checks every database entry for a type that matches.  A key
    design issue is that the EvType cycle FSM only knows about the 3 types, while the database
    FSM only knows about the database and hides the database methodology from the cycle FSM.
    Multiple similar Events within this Agency Root occur in an order determined by the database.
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Agency Root does not care how a database is organized or manipulated, it just wants an Event
    with an Agency Api FSM active, which is required in order to have the Agency Run FSM active.
    There is a priority between event Types (Ireq, Data, Time; in descending priority) and there
    may be a priority between Events within a type (as implementation of AgencyNext determines).
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    EvTypeFSM_state = ssE_EvType_Ireq;
//
    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    A programming model for a looping mechanism which has complex and/or multiple exit critera
    can be implemented as "set a flag and continue to find flag" or "break out of while now".
    Software Engineering argues against this in coding standards; ssTEA's goal is readable.
    -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    The K&R ssHL-language construct is "call the function, assign return value to variable, compare
    return value in variable to a value, enter loop if resolution is: values are not equal".
    The parentheses '(' and ')' pairing is correct to implement this construct: it forces
    the assignment to pEvInfo to complete first, then that value is compared to Null.
    Leaving out the parenthesis causes pEvInfo to be assigned the result of a != comparison.
    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    everything within the "while" begin/end is in the context of a valid pEvInfo/ssE_pAboutEv.
    In addition, we know that the database returned an event of type requested, so actions
    are taken without consideration of error conditions or values out of range and invalid.
    Features associated with each Type while being manipulated by ssA are implemented here.
    -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    while (true)
    {
        while ((pEvInfo = ssA_EvAg_AgencyNext (pEvInfo, EvTypeFSM_state)) != ssE_pEvInfoNull)
//
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   non-Time Event types have been handled before this point; this one, by definition, Time.
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   if (ssE_pAboutEv->Runfsm_EvType != ssE_EvType_Time)
       switch (ssE_pAboutEv->AgencyResult)
//
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Event Agency itself, as represented in the data structures, is always interpreted anew.
   Those values are OccursAt, Period, and Recurs; an Event may change in any combination:
        a new OccursAt Time in the future at which it wants to be granted Agency,
        the fact that the event is recurring or not recurring
        the period that will be added to a Time (using a rule) for a recurring event
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The Time event has occured at the Time requested, and the event thought it all went OK.
   The state of the Run FSM must have been "Agencying" for Agency to have been granted.
   The Event may change its Run FSM state to Stopped or Paused, whether Recurring or not.
   A Time event may stay in the agencying state after changing any values defining Events.
   Recall that only Events of type Time are under consideration here.
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   switch (ssE_pAboutEv->AgencyResult)
//
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   When recursFromTrue, the TimeCurr value given to the Event on Agency is "the base".
     this has the effect of allowing variations in the Pace Period to affect OccursAt.
   When not recursFromTrue, the time requested (OccursAt) for the Event is "the base".
      this has the effect of preventing slew/jitter/noise in the timing of Event agency.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   if the event recurs, the period is added to the selected base; no states are changed.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   An event may refer to and change its own configuration.   For example, an Event is
   allowed to change its own one-time OccursAt, as a form of a cascading periodic event.
   Note that the self-Resume of an Event changing its own OccursAt requires a future Time.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   take no action with respect to the Run FSM state, only adjust OccursAt using Period.
   The math does not check or filter any values in "the base"
       Actual: continue recurring 100ms from now (605ms), set OccursAt to 705ms.
      !Actual: continue recurring 100ms from requested (600ms), OccursAt gets 700ms.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   if (ssE_pAboutEv->recurs)
       pTime = (ssE_pAboutEv->recursFromTrue) ? ssT_gpTime_Current : &ssE_pAboutEv->OccursAt;
//
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   insert Monty Python Dead Parrot Sketch, an Agencying Event has occured, now it is dead.
   If your event doesn't want to be dead, put a million volts through it.  Then... Voom!
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   an event that was only intended to occur run once has occured at the Time requested, AND,
   the event occurrence returned a normal result to the ssTEA Agency grantor, AND,
   the Event owner did not Stop/Pause the Event, leaving it in Agencying state in Run FSM.
   Stop the event if OccursAt has not changed during the event, the most normal conclusion.
   Continue the EVENT if Event's OccurAt has been changed by the Event itself, a feature.
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   A dying Event is flipped to pending through the Agency post-Event grant processing: in
   that the test above ("greater than") skips pending events, this test ("not greater than")
   catches events that have an OccursAt not greater than the Current Time (just Agencied).
   An Event with OccursAt changed to a valid future Time is allowed to continute agencying.
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   if (ssT_timeIf_P1equalsORafterP2 (&ssE_pAboutEv->OccursAt, ssT_gpTime_Current))
//
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   if the Event changed the OccursAt value, Event "chose" to automatically keep Agencying.
   This is a feature of ssTEA, but the value of OccursAt has to be a valid value, and the
   Time value is going to often be the result of blind math operation with full faith.  The
   OccursAt value may be changed at the same time as the recurs indicator, because any
   transition from direct/recurring to recurring/direct happens by definition at Curr Time.
   Said another way, an Event comes back from Agency with a blank slate in ssTEA's view.
   Note that the filter is that the value is a valid Time value, which includes -/0/+ range.
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   if (!ssE_pAboutEv->OccursAt.Valid)
//
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   All event instances of one type have been checked for this Agency Root instance.
   Because this is Agency Root, there is no knowledge of the organization of the database.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Modifications to types and states may occur when Events are granted agency.  Thus an
   Ireq event can change its own type to Data, and then that same event will run (as Data).
   a Data Event may trigger an Event of type Time by modifying the Occurs At for the Event.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   The ability to do this directly requires building ssTEA such that all event data
   allocations occur only one time and are shared between the application and ssTEA.

   The !TRUSTED model of building requires that a user check about event's current state:
    1) API calls from Events while being granted Agency change the database.
    2) API calls from the App and not within granted Agency change the database.
   This is accomplished by using the API to request the current state.

   The TRUSTED model of building makes all modifications to a single shared live copy.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   if (EvTypeFSM_state == ssE_EvType_Ireq)
       if (EvTypeFSM_state == ssE_EvType_Data)
           if (EvTypeFSM_state == ssE_EvType_Time)
//

// S~S  SimpleSal signal ends  S~S
